jadx-rs
Copyright 2026 the jadx-rs contributors

This project is a Rust reimplementation of the decompiler engine of jadx
(https://github.com/skylot/jadx), Copyright 2015 Skylot and contributors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The algorithms, pass ordering and data-model structure follow the original
jadx design; the original Java sources are used as a behavioural reference
(oracle) and are not part of this repository.

crates/jadx-core/resources/core.jcst is the class hierarchy data of the Android and Java
framework classes shipped with jadx (Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2015 Skylot and contributors).

crates/jadx-mcp (the MCP server) contains code adapted from RDX, Copyright 2026 Ch0pin and RDX
contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
RDX itself includes code adapted from JADX (Skylot and contributors) and Android Open Source Project
material under their respective licenses. The adapted parts of RDX are its MCP (Model Context
Protocol) server design; no GUI, plugin window, screenshot, Frida or bundled font, icon or theme
material was taken. Modifications relative to RDX:

  - crates/jadx-mcp/src/protocol.rs: newline delimited JSON-RPC framing, the frame size limit with
    the RESPONSE_TOO_LARGE fallback and the request validation and serve loop of the RDX stdio
    gateway. Rewritten to be generic over any reader and writer, with a separate request reader so
    that cancellation notifications are seen during a running tool call; the GUI worker, loopback
    TCP service, instance registry and discovery code were not carried over.
  - crates/jadx-mcp/src/server.rs: lifecycle handling (initialize, ping, tools/list, tools/call) and
    the shape of tool results (text content plus structuredContent, coded errors). Reworked for a
    single shared project per process instead of GUI instances.
  - crates/jadx-mcp/src/registry.rs: the declarative tool table, JSON schema generation, parameter
    aliases and argument validation (unknown arguments reported with the accepted names, selector
    alternatives). Reduced to the parameter model this server needs and re-expressed as a typed
    ToolSpec.
  - crates/jadx-mcp/src/args.rs: list paging (items, total, next_offset), text paging by Unicode
    scalar offset with a source hash for change detection, and alias conflict rules. A different hash
    function and error type are used.
  - crates/jadx-mcp/src/index.rs: class selector resolution (exact id, descriptor form, unique short
    name, ambiguity and "did you mean" candidates). Reimplemented over the project class table of
    this repository.
  - The tool surface (class listing and search, class source, method source, disassembly, manifest
    and resource access, string search, hierarchy and usage queries) follows the tool names and
    conventions documented by RDX; every tool is implemented anew on top of the engine crates of this
    repository.

RDX is distributed without per-file license headers; the attribution above and the header comments
of the adapted modules take their place.

Further parts adapted from RDX (Copyright 2026 Ch0pin and RDX contributors, Apache License,
Version 2.0), Rust non-GUI engine code; each adapted file names its origin and the modifications
in its module documentation:

- crates/jadx-package: the split-package container reader (bundletool `toc.pb` reader, split
  identity validation, logical split-aware entry paths, bounded ZIP directory check, temporary
  APK handling) is adapted from RDX `src/package_container.rs`. Modifications: the selection
  policy of the reference jadx plugins as default, `.apkm` support, manifest decoding with
  `jadx-resources`, a dependency free JSON reader, no dependency on the RDX engine.
- crates/jadx-index: the posting store (fingerprint keyed fixed size records, sorted runs on disk
  merged into one file that lookups binary-search) is adapted from RDX `src/invoke_index.rs`; the
  package scope filter from `src/package_scope.rs`; the bounded call graph (depth, node and edge
  caps, component classification, dispatch targets) from `src/call_graph.rs`; the call site, field
  access and integer literal scans from `src/native_xrefs.rs`, `src/field_references.rs` and
  `src/integer_references.rs`; the name and literal search ideas from `src/identifier_search.rs`
  and `src/search.rs`. Modifications: the index works on the `jadx-core` root and on instructions
  decoded by `jadx-dex-input` instead of the RDX engine, uses a dependency free fingerprint, a
  memory budget with external merge, and verifies every hit against the decoded code.

No fonts, icons, themes or GUI code of RDX are part of this repository.
